      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Tricky feature of the day where the headline horse is COSMIC CRUSADER (1) who makes his Melbourne debut. He went through the grades in fine fashion over the Perth carnival, beating the Railway winner Watch Me Rock in the G1 Northerly Stakes before dropping back to 1400m a week later and charging home to split Rey Magnerio & Overpass. That form is miles clear of these and if he's just sharp enough at 1200m he could be too good. ZOU SENSATION (3) might be the value. He didn't really fire in two runs up North but his best form reads very well for this, albeit his best trip is 1400m. Respecting while fresh. Out of the horses through the John Monash, MIRAVAL ROSE (8) might be the improver. She'll want further again but the extra 100m and added fitness suits. WINNASEDGE (7) won that under a good ride and 1200m is no issue for him, he'll be up on speed and looks a big chance for the double. WATCHME WIN (6) got home well in the Monash and should be thereabouts again.",
